.TH VIEWDI 1 "" "viewDI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viewdi \- manage and monitor Docker and Incus from one terminal UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viewdi
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B viewdi doctor
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B viewdi completion
\fBbash\fR|\fBzsh\fR|\fBfish\fR
.br
.B viewdi man
.SH DESCRIPTION
viewDI manages and monitors Docker and Incus side by side from one terminal UI: lifecycle, one card per app on a Home screen, a machines list and tree, an activity feed, logs, metrics, image and engine updates.
.PP
viewDI only reads from the update sources and never installs anything. It talks to the daemons through their sockets, so it needs the same group membership as the docker and incus command line tools (\fBdocker\fR, and \fBincus\-admin\fR or \fBincus\fR). Press \fB?\fR inside viewDI for the key map.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mock\fR[=\fIvalue\fR]
use fake engines instead of real daemons; optional scenario: [homelab large chaos logflood offline] (write \-\-mock=<scenario>)
.TP
\fB\-\-mock\-notify\fR
with \-\-mock, send desktop notifications for the mock updates (never sent in \-\-mock otherwise)
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-only\fR
disable every mutating action (monitoring only)
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
write a debug log to the state directory and enable the ctrl+d overlay
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR[=\fIvalue\fR]
record every UI message to a file for replay (write \-\-trace=<file>; default under the state directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-pprof\fR \fIvalue\fR
serve pprof on a loopback address, e.g. 127.0.0.1:6060
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fIvalue\fR
theme ID for this session (overrides state.json and config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR \fIvalue\fR
metrics refresh interval, 250ms\(en2s (overrides config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-docker\-host\fR \fIvalue\fR
Docker daemon URI (overrides DOCKER_HOST)
.TP
\fB\-\-incus\-socket\fR \fIvalue\fR
Incus unix socket path (overrides INCUS_SOCKET)
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
print the version and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-update\fR
update viewDI to the latest release and exit (downloads from GitHub, checks the checksum, asks first)
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
with \-\-update: do not ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-update: reinstall the same version, or replace a development build
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check the Docker and Incus sockets, whether this session may use them, the terminal and the optional tools, and print how to fix each problem. Exits 1 when neither engine can be reached. It accepts \fB\-\-docker\-host\fR and \fB\-\-incus\-socket\fR.
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR \fIshell\fR
Print the completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
.TP
\fBman\fR
Print this manual page.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B viewdi
manage the real Docker and Incus daemons
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-read\-only
look but do not touch: every mutating action is disabled
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-mock
try it without any daemon, on made\-up containers
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-mock=chaos
watch the UI survive failing daemons
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-docker\-host ssh://me@server
a remote Docker daemon over SSH
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-theme nord \-\-refresh 2s
pick a theme and a slower metrics refresh
.TP
.B viewdi doctor
check sockets, permissions and optional tools, and say how to fix what is missing
.TP
.B viewdi \-\-debug
also write the debug level to ~/.local/state/viewDI/viewdi.log (warnings and errors are always written there)
.TP
.B viewdi completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/viewdi.fish
install the completions
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/viewDI/config.toml
settings, edited by hand and never rewritten by viewDI
.TP
.I ~/.config/viewDI/themes/*.toml
your own themes
.TP
.I ~/.config/viewDI/keys.toml
key overrides
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/viewDI/state.json
last view, theme, sort, folded tree nodes
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/viewDI/viewdi.log
warnings, errors and failed actions; \-\-debug adds the debug level
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/viewDI/crash\-*.log
crash reports
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/viewDI/labs.json
your labs
.TP
.I ~/.cache/viewDI/updates.json
update check cache
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Docker daemon URI (default: the rootless socket, then /var/run/docker.sock)
.TP
.B DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY
set when a tcp:// Docker host uses TLS; without it viewDI warns
.TP
.B INCUS_SOCKET
path of the Incus unix socket
.TP
.B INCUS_DIR
directory holding unix.socket (default /var/lib/incus, then /run/incus)
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
raises the GitHub API rate limit of the engine update checks
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
use the colourless monochrome theme and no terminal colour queries
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
move the files above
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
An error, or a crash (the path of the crash report is printed).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
